{"$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"pmat"}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":false,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"error","message":{"text":"pmat query/index probe (bounded 90s, systemd-run unit a57-pmat-1790429918) did not complete; host load average measured at 78.17/66.73/62.76 (uptime), many competing sessions holding the shared cargo-wrapper flock and active cargo build jobs (ps aux). Unit stopped rather than left queued."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["pmat","query","row errors","--limit","3"],"exit_code":143}},{"level":"error","message":{"text":"cargo test -p aprender-review-experiment --lib (systemd-run unit a57-rv3-1790428731) queued 14+ minutes on the shared cargo wrapper flock under the same measured host contention; stopped rather than forced through. Refactor soundness for admission.rs and receipt.rs was instead confirmed by manual diff review (see PRREV-4431-RESTAMP-REFACTOR-SOUND)."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["cargo","test","-p","aprender-review-experiment","--lib"]}}],"properties":{"transport":"cli","transport_unavailable":["cli: query/index probe timed out under host contention"]}}],"results":[{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-GHOST-BINDING-MSE-SPLIT","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Re-verified against crates/aprender-core/src/tree/regression_helpers.rs:27 for this round: a function named compute_mse with the exact claimed signature (y_left: &[f32], y_right: &[f32]) -> f32) does exist, but at module path aprender::tree::regression_helpers and visibility pub(super), not the binding's declared aprender::tree::helpers / public. The binding's module_path is wrong and the function is not reachable at the path it claims, despite status: implemented."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/aprender/binding.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":188}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"cited","precision_class":"advisory","carried_forward_from":"evidence/pr-review/4431/0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22/findings.sarif","failure_scenario":"A caller resolves the binding's declared path aprender::tree::helpers::compute_mse expecting a public implemented function; that path does not exist (real fn is pub(super) under tree::regression_helpers), so any generated binding or doc built from this contract entry fails to compile or silently points nowhere.","source":"contracts/aprender/binding.yaml:187-192","excerpt":"- contract: decision-tree-v1.yaml\n  equation: mse_split\n  module_path: aprender::tree::helpers\n  function: compute_mse\n  signature: 'fn compute_mse(y_left: &[f32], y_right: &[f32]) -> f32'\n  status: implemented","excerpt_sha256":"5d05143e46a7126d4e91b6e38eeeb24600b1efe7a1e973f479fcbe4a070bce6b"}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-GHOST-BINDING-PAGERANK","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Re-verified against crates/aprender-core/src/graph/centrality.rs:64,128 for this round: module path aprender::graph::centrality and function name pagerank do exist, but as a trait method fn pagerank(&self, damping: f64, max_iter: usize, tol: f64) -> Result<Vec<f64>, String>, not the binding's declared free function fn pagerank(adj: &Tensor, damping: f64, max_iter: usize, tol: f64) -> Tensor. The extra adj parameter and the Tensor return type are not backed by any implementation, despite status: implemented."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/aprender/binding.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":32}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"cited","precision_class":"advisory","carried_forward_from":"evidence/pr-review/4431/0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22/findings.sarif","failure_scenario":"Code or docs generated from the binding's declared signature fn pagerank(adj: &Tensor, ...) -> Tensor will not compile against the real Graph::pagerank(&self, ...) -> Result<Vec<f64>, String>; a caller trusting status: implemented for that exact signature hits a build failure or, if hand-adapted, silently drops the Result's error path.","source":"contracts/aprender/binding.yaml:31-36","excerpt":"- contract: pagerank-kernel-v1.yaml\n  equation: pagerank\n  module_path: aprender::graph::centrality\n  function: Graph::pagerank\n  signature: 'fn pagerank(adj: &Tensor, damping: f64, max_iter: usize, tol: f64) -> Tensor'\n  status: implemented","excerpt_sha256":"4d173ea1a016b1121037edc17161a379cf1c026b37de21554ff215fbaf2b8509"}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-RESTAMP-REFACTOR-SOUND","level":"note","message":{"text":"admission.rs row_errors() and receipt.rs problems() were split into cell_errors/field_errors/status_errors and named_problems/sha_problems/execution_problems respectively; git diff confirms call order and all message text are byte-identical to the pre-refactor functions (pure extract-function, complexity-ratchet motivated)."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"crates/aprender-review-experiment/src/admission.rs"},"region":{"startLine":1}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"crates/aprender-review-experiment/src/receipt.rs"},"region":{"startLine":1}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["git","diff","0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22","8b59fe3016a17b41a832eacebe0e1c9b333d44d8","--","crates/aprender-review-experiment/src/admission.rs","crates/aprender-review-experiment/src/receipt.rs"],"exit_code":0,"precision_class":"advisory","failure_scenario":"If the split of row_errors()/problems() had reordered calls or altered a message, callers of admission.rs/receipt.rs would get wrong error text or dropped errors; the byte-identical diff rules this out for this delta."}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-RESTAMP-RETIRED-SCRIPT-NO-DANGLING-REF","level":"note","message":{"text":"scripts/ci_run_target_release.sh was renamed to scripts/retired/ci_run_target_release.sh (0 diff lines, byte-identical move, sha256 6e8f49c0... on both sides). A live-surface grep of .github/, scripts/guard_tree.sh, scripts/check_*.sh, and ci/ (excluding scripts/retired) finds zero remaining references. Remaining hits are documentation and history files only."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/retired/ci_run_target_release.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["git","grep","-n","ci_run_target_release","--",".",":!scripts/retired/*"],"exit_code":0,"precision_class":"advisory","failure_scenario":"If a live surface (.github/, guard_tree.sh, check_*.sh, ci/) still referenced the old scripts/ci_run_target_release.sh path, CI would fail to find the script after the rename; the grep found zero such references."}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-RESTAMP-GUARD-ADAPTATIONS-PASS","level":"note","message":{"text":"The 4 pr-review guard scripts adapted for the #4433 ci.yml to ci/sections.yml fat-jobs split each pass their own --self-test in full: check_pr_review_arm4.sh 23/23, check_pr_review_counts.sh 16/16, check_pr_review_wiring.sh 13/13, check_guards_are_wired.sh 14/14."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/check_pr_review_arm4.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/check_pr_review_counts.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/check_pr_review_wiring.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/check_guards_are_wired.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["bash","scripts/check_pr_review_arm4.sh","--self-test"],"exit_code":0,"precision_class":"advisory","failure_scenario":"If any of the 4 pr-review guard scripts mis-adapted to the ci.yml -> ci/sections.yml fat-jobs split, their own --self-test cases would fail and the guard would silently stop enforcing on the new layout; all 66 cases pass."}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-RESTAMP-LADDER-MUTANTS-PASS","level":"note","message":{"text":"check_ladder_cells_producer.sh owed-set mutant line changed from list(J.owed_rungs(...))[:1] to zip(J.owed_rungs(...), range(1)) (behaviorally equivalent). --self-test confirms all 8 cases and all 6 mutants (needle, fallback, retry, owed-set, refusal, think) still pass and kill correctly."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/check_ladder_cells_producer.sh"},"region":{"startLine":1}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["bash","scripts/check_ladder_cells_producer.sh","--self-test"],"exit_code":0,"precision_class":"advisory","failure_scenario":"If the owed-set rewrite (list(...)[:1] -> zip(..., range(1))) were not behaviorally equivalent, check_ladder_cells_producer.sh's mutant-kill cases would silently accept a bad ladder cell; --self-test confirms all 8 cases and 6 mutants still pass/kill."}},{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-VS-COUNT-TESTED-EXCEEDS-TOTAL","level":"error","message":{"text":"Carried forward unchanged from the prior receipt (0644f9c08): 8 contracts under contracts/ report a verification_summary tested or proven count exceeding total_obligations. None of these files were changed in 0644f9c08..8b59fe301 (git diff --stat over the exact 8 paths is empty), so the finding stands as-is."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/apr-cli-qa-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":256}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/apr-docs-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":161}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/apr-dogfood-coverage-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":851}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/crate-hygiene-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":128}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/crate-readme-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":60}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/hero-svg-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":67}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/ratatui-migration-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":88}}},{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"contracts/unified-specs-v1.yaml"},"region":{"startLine":82}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","precision_class":"advisory","carried_forward_from":"evidence/pr-review/4431/0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22/findings.sarif","failure_scenario":"A contract reporting tested/proven counts above total_obligations lets a consumer of that contract's verification_summary believe more was verified than the obligation set allows, masking a bookkeeping defect in the 8 affected contract files."}}]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"nvidia-cuda-docs"}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":false,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"error","message":{"text":"Carried forward unchanged from the prior receipt: agent cuda-docs-reviewer not available and mcp nvidia-cuda-docs needs OAuth the non-interactive session cannot run. This delta's only cuda-path-matching files (crates/aprender-serve/src/cuda/executor/*, gguf/cuda/forward_qwen35_cuda*.rs) were confirmed byte-identical to origin/main via git diff --stat (carried over verbatim by the merge commit e5929e6e5, not authored by this fold branch) -- no new device-behaviour claim to check."}}]}],"results":[]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"crux"}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[]}],"results":[{"ruleId":"PRREV-4431-BUILD-VERIFY-RESOLVED","level":"note","message":{"text":"Carried forward from evidence/pr-review/4431/0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22: that round re-ran cargo test -p aprender-contracts --lib to completion (2007 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored, 207.10s) to resolve a prior DEGRADED gap where two attempts had been killed under host contention. This delta (8b59fe301..7061eb6dd1, evidence-only) introduces no new build-verification surface, so the measured result stands unchanged."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"crates/aprender-review-experiment/src/admission.rs"},"region":{"startLine":1}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","precision_class":"advisory","carried_forward_from":"evidence/pr-review/4431/0644f9c083264f86a4201cd122e64498fa90af22/findings.sarif","failure_scenario":"Had this cargo test run not been re-executed to completion, a reviewer would have to trust an unverified self-report of '2002/2002 passing' from an earlier round whose own verification attempts were killed under host contention; the measured re-run (2007 passed/0 failed) closes that gap.","command":["cargo","test","-p","aprender-contracts","--lib"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":"5251ff04fe8f7e4aba9901d72bdd3c6d961ce00fd4f07652e2777de8532f5032","rationale_for_class":"Resolves a prior DEGRADED build-verification gap; not itself a defect."}}]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"cargo-mutants"}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[]}],"results":[]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"antigravity"}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":false,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"error","message":{"text":"Not dispatched in this restamp: the parent task instructions did not include an agy/antigravity round, and the host was under severe measured contention throughout this session (see pmat run notifications). attempted: 0."}}]}],"results":[]}]}
